{
  "manufacturer": "Lumel",
  "manufacturer_slug": "lumel",
  "model": "NR10PLUS single-phase energy meter",
  "model_slug": "nr10plus",
  "short_model": "NR10PLUS",
  "aliases": [
    "NR10PLUS"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Energy meter (DIN-rail, single-phase)",
  "applies_to": "Lumel NR10PLUS single-phase DIN-rail meter with RS-485 Modbus RTU, per its user manual.",
  "summary": "Single-phase DIN-rail energy counter with pulse outputs and an RS-485 Modbus RTU port. Values are IEEE-754 floats in two registers, high word first, readable as input registers (3X) and mirrored as holding registers (4X). The map covers instantaneous values, demands, import/export, tariff and partial energies, run hours and status values.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The measurement table prints Modicon numbers (30001) next to the hex start address (00 00). The hex column is the wire address, so 30001 is register 0 and power factor 30031 is 0x1E."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "NR10PLUS Single Phase AC Energy Meter - User Manual",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.lumel.com.pl/resources/Pliki%20do%20pobrania/NR10PLUS/NR10PLUS_user_manual.pdf",
    "pages": "RS-485 section and example frames pp. 15-17; Table 4 3X/4X measured parameters pp. 17-21 (printed page numbers)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Format is stated as 4 bytes per parameter, IEEE-754 float, most significant byte first; the example frames return 43 66 00 00 for 230 V and 40 A0 00 00 for 5 A, which settles high word first.",
    "The same values sit in the 4X (holding register) area at the same addresses; this map lists the 3X copy only.",
    "Left out: 0x54, labelled 'var Exp. Max Demand' exactly like 0x56; the long-energy table (0x200 on) because its format is not spelled out; the 4X setup table and the assignable area.",
    "Energy registers count up to 99999.999 and the matching overflow register counts the roll-overs.",
    "Left out: 0x102 'Power Fail Status', printed with unit W and no value meanings."
  ],
